UNATTRIBUTED  ast-V8Base.json: Was in neither this backlog nor provenance/, which is an omission rather than a signal: every other tracked AST is accounted for one way or the other, and this one was simply never listed. It entered the tree in df77544 (2026-08-25, '285 tracked theorems were pinned to a corpus no clone could see'), which tracked the AST precisely so a clone could see the corpus. Same gap as ast-V8Numbers.json: the V8 tree and revision are not identified and the CPG was not kept, so reproduction was not attempted. Closing this needs the V8 revision recorded and a re-export from it.
UNATTRIBUTED  ast-V8BaseSample.json: Not a Joern export: an EXTRACTION. All 4 entries were verified byte-identical to their (name, file) counterparts in ast-V8Base.json, which is gitignored and local-only. Commit 5fd17ae describes it as the call-closure of the functions Autoform/SpecsGen/V8BaseSample.lean names. No extraction script is committed, so there is no exact command to record, and naming cartographer/export_ast.sc plus a V8 source tree would claim a regeneration path that does not produce this file. Attribution requires committing the extractor (and recording the parent AST it selects from).
UNATTRIBUTED  ast-V8Numbers.json: Regenerated by 52a6987 (2026-08-21, 'Wire float literals to Float.lean'), which is how the digest moved off the earlier baseline. Reproduction NOT attempted: the entries come from V8's conversions.cc, hash-seed.cc, ieee754.cc and math-random.cc, and neither the V8 tree nor its revision is identified anywhere in this repository, nor was the CPG kept. This is the weakest class of entry here -- it names when the artifact changed and under which commit, not what it was built from. Unlike ast-Cachetools.json, whose revision was recovered by matching a fresh export's function set, a C++ corpus of this size cannot be identified that way cheaply. Closing this needs the V8 revision recorded and a re-export from it.
